  "details": "sometimes avatars load just fine. but then there is sometimes where i am in the instance, for a while, the avatar's will show that they are downloading. progress makes it to a random progress then stop. will sit at that percentage for hours and refuse to move! i have tried exiting the instance and go to another instance aka home then return back to that instance in hopes the avatars load. the progress will restart and it maybe will load but most of the time will get stuck! only way i found to fix is to close completly out of vr chat and relaunch it! pc performance not affected as i got plenty of ram. \n\nmy pc has 16gb of ram total (when not in vrc, i am only using 4gb so all that ram left over goes to vrc.) and storage isnt a problem as i got 4x 1tb ssd's in raid 0) i also tried to uninstall and reinstall vrc, i even used revo to uninstall and clear cache. i went into the vrc files and del avatar cache data to no sucess! i talked to few ppl and they tell me that it does same thing to them. i do notice tho that it happens when there is ALOT of ppl on at one time. maybe it is a download que problem? to many downloading at once from the que? i have a symetrical 100 megabit connection so internet not the problem. it is very annoying that avatars isnt loading when i trying to moderate a instance also as i can not see if avatar is nsfw. or is a \"crasher\" avatar!",
